{"kind":"artifact","text":"notes/2026-10-04-authority-effects-and-publication.md at exact 8b1c3c9d7987fba6ac5f5b31fbe329d50a3f568b on request/authority-r20, under promise git:sha1…03174d7 on request git:sha1…535c941\n\nAuthority, effects and publication, revision 28 at 8b1c3c9d7987fba6ac5f5b31fbe329d50a3f568b on request/authority-r20, for my request eee603c6, answering the checker's changes-requested verdict af0d0a5e on 1f3cfca5. Primary subject: notes/2026-10-04-authority-effects-and-publication.md. Design only; nothing was run; sizes and counts are sums by script. P2 1 is repaired by eight rules on a write's target, which is closed when the write can no longer act: a confirmed mint sets the token slot only when its attempt has no outcome and the target is open; otherwise its own outcome records the token and its end and opens the revocation with no slot set; an entry that closes a target touches no token; the gateway sends only while the slot names the mint and the target is open. No guard is added to resend-receipt, so recovery never waits on a read. A late token's record stands in the mint's own confirmed outcome entry, and a derived read lists tokens for an operator. Each revocation is for the holder of its mint, which reserved it with the mint; no entry of one holder opens a revocation for another, and no count in section 5.8 changes. Both serial orders and the control are worked as tables with witness rows. The sweep of the fault's family covers 30 outcome rules and result clauses of the destination, the register and the directory; six needed the same repair (the mint for a receipt, for a push after a resend and an older read, and for a first head after an adopt-head; the token step of a push on a final publication and of a receipt on a final receipt; and adopt-read answering after a reservation), each with a witness row; membership, the rules scope, the inbox and the task scope were not swept. P2 2 is repaired: reserve gains a sixth field, reports, of at most 32 typed facts, bound place by place to the manifest's selections, with a mismatch not reserved, evidence-invalid; each report's commit is derived from its retained entry in judge and in replay; the count is 2 + v + j + d + r, the ceiling v + j + d + r of at most 126 stays under the contract's 128, and a reserve over it is refused bad-field with nothing fetched; duplicate and source policies are tabled. Both size tables are recomputed whole with no guessed allowance: the judge's outcome sums to 236,087 bytes and the delivery of reserve to 193,612, against 262,144, with 65 authors and 8 keys kept; three values have no declared bound and are stated as assumptions (the run ID, the form of a time, and prepared). The planner's answers of 53ecfb42 are applied. The index on the publication's operation slot is stated in the form of contract revision 23, effective only when a contract revision carrying it is adopted; revision 19 is the adopted contract. Three new asks go to the contract, the chief one a send source that gives one member of each record of a list, without which the lane cannot send reports as typed; two asks go to the lane forms; three questions go to the planner. The Git test vectors remain unchecked with Git and are carried to the source's witness on a real repository. Counts by script: 129 rows in section 14, 20 cases in 12.1.5, marks unchanged.","body":{"commit":"8b1c3c9d7987fba6ac5f5b31fbe329d50a3f568b","path":"notes/2026-10-04-authority-effects-and-publication.md"}}